Fix the admin container failing to start with a PostgreSQL database (`ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'psycopg'`). SQLAlchemy 2.1 selects psycopg 3 for `postgresql://` URIs, so the image now ships psycopg 3 instead of psycopg2. `DB_FLAVOR=postgresql` and a `SQLALCHEMY_DATABASE_URI` starting with `postgresql://` work unchanged; a URI that names the old driver explicitly (`postgresql+psycopg2://`) has to drop the `+psycopg2`.
